  "slug": "arabidopsis-mediated-f99c",
  "summary": "New Plant Physiology papers dissect specific regulators of ABA turnover, ROS signaling and JA-driven senescence across crops and Arabidopsis.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is mechanistic control of hormone metabolism and ROS signaling in stress and development. On the ABA axis, GhNAC029 represses GhNCED1 to lower ABA and drought tolerance in cotton. In Brassica, methylation of the BraCYP707A3.A02 promoter blocks BraBPC2.A08 binding, linking ABA catabolism to clubroot resistance. ANAC030 promotes Arabidopsis leaf senescence via JA biosynthesis, programmed cell death and chlorophyll metabolism. ROS-centred modules span contexts. In apple, MxMPK4-1 phosphorylates NADP-malic enzyme MxME3-7 at S201 to enhance ROS-mediated iron-deficiency responses. In pear, PUB8 degrades ZAT11/12, which activate LAC1 for ROS-linked lignification and stone cell formation. Post-translational and post-transcriptional layers recur: a preprint couples H2S persulfidation and PRMT5-dependent LSm4 methylation to alternative splicing in stomatal closure, and miR159a cleavage of BrMYB12 reduces myo-inositol/raffinose synthesis and thermotolerance. Ursolic acid limits fresh-cut apple browning through MdMYB70/MdbHLH62 control of ascorbate.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
